From 6cf41afd5bb7ce187f415146750a60d18d90f1c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Arrendondo <brandon.arrendondo@bissell.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 21:32:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] AP: Fix OOB read of STA's HE-MCS map in check_valid_he_mcs()

check_valid_he_mcs() reads sta_mcs_set[i * 4] for i in [0, mcs_count),
where sta_mcs_set points into the "Supported HE-MCS And NSS Set" field
of the STA's HE Capabilities element and mcs_count (1, 2, or 3) is
derived entirely from the AP's own configured he_oper_chwidth. Nothing
bounds i against the actual length of the STA-supplied element: a STA
that sends a minimum-length (21-byte, HE_CAPABILITIES_ELEM_MIN_LEN) HE
Capabilities element while the AP is configured for 160 MHz (or 80+80
MHz) HE operation causes a read past the end of that element's buffer.

copy_sta_he_capab() does call ieee80211_invalid_he_cap_size(), which
validates he_capab_len, but that check is not sufficient on its own: it
derives the length it requires from the PHY Capabilities Info bits the
STA itself declared in the same element, not from the AP's
he_oper_chwidth. A STA can simply not set the corresponding
channel-width bits and still pass that check at the element's minimum
length, while check_valid_he_mcs() keeps reading based on the AP's
independently configured operating width.

Pass he_capab_len into check_valid_he_mcs() and stop the loop before
reading an MCS map field the element is too short to actually contain.

Signed-off-by: Brandon Arrendondo <brandon.arrendondo@bissell.com>
(cherry picked from commit 6cf41afd5bb7ce187f415146750a60d18d90f1c9)
---
 src/ap/ieee802_11_he.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ap/ieee802_11_he.c b/src/ap/ieee802_11_he.c
index bc0b50c6e..f09f51399 100644
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11_he.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11_he.c
@@ -411,6 +411,7 @@ void hostapd_get_he_capab(struct hostapd_data *hapd,
 
 
 static int check_valid_he_mcs(struct hostapd_data *hapd, const u8 *sta_he_capab,
+			      size_t sta_he_capab_len,
 			      enum ieee80211_op_mode opmode)
 {
 	u16 sta_rx_mcs_set, ap_tx_mcs_set;
@@ -446,6 +447,16 @@ static int check_valid_he_mcs(struct hostapd_data *hapd, const u8 *sta_he_capab,
 	for (i = 0; i < mcs_count; i++) {
 		int j;
 
+		/* mcs_count (and hence the highest i reached here) is
+		 * derived from the AP's own configured operating channel
+		 * width, not from anything the STA guarantees about the
+		 * length of its HE Capabilities element. Stop before
+		 * reading an MCS map field the STA's element is too short
+		 * to actually contain. */
+		if ((size_t) (IEEE80211_HE_CAPAB_MIN_LEN + (i + 1) * 4) >
+		    sta_he_capab_len)
+			break;
+
 		/* AP Tx MCS map vs. STA Rx MCS map */
 		sta_rx_mcs_set = WPA_GET_LE16(&sta_mcs_set[i * 4]);
 		ap_tx_mcs_set = WPA_GET_LE16((const u8 *)
@@ -475,7 +486,7 @@ u16 copy_sta_he_capab(struct hostapd_data *hapd, struct sta_info *sta,
 {
 	if (!he_capab || !(sta->flags & WLAN_STA_WMM) ||
 	    !hostapd_is_he_enabled(hapd) ||
-	    !check_valid_he_mcs(hapd, he_capab, opmode) ||
+	    !check_valid_he_mcs(hapd, he_capab, he_capab_len, opmode) ||
 	    ieee80211_invalid_he_cap_size(he_capab, he_capab_len) ||
 	    he_capab_len > sizeof(struct ieee80211_he_capabilities)) {
 		sta->flags &= ~WLAN_STA_HE;
